Prevention as referred to in article 5 letter a, includes: collecting data and information about women victims of violence as well as laws and regulations;
conducting education about anti-violence values towards women;
socializing laws and regulations related to the implementation of protection for women victims of violence;
establishing and facilitating the implementation of integrated service institutions for women victims by involving community elements;
encouraging community awareness of the importance of protection for women victims of violence;
Increasing women's awareness of the importance of complying with ethics, religious norms and cultural norms in behavior.
Prevention as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out by the Regional Government of the Regency, police institutions, prosecutorial institutions, judicial institutions, non-governmental organizations, and the community in accordance with their duties, functions, and responsibilities.

