CHAPTER III
OBLIGATIONS OF REGIONAL GOVERNMENT
Article 4
Regional government in implementing protection of women from acts of violence has the following obligations: to formulate strategic plans for protection of women against acts of violence for the short, medium, and long term as an integrated part of the Regional Medium-Term Development Plan (RPJMD);
to prevent and handle in an integrated manner the occurrence of acts of violence against women;
to encourage the responsibility of police institutions, prosecutorial institutions, judicial institutions, non-governmental organizations, religious institutions, and the general public to conduct coordination and cooperation in carrying out prevention and handling of the occurrence of acts of violence against women;
to optimize the role and function of institutions within the regional government environment related to carrying out prevention and handling of protection of women from acts of violence;
to provide facilities and infrastructure;
to conduct guidance, supervision and evaluation.

