to optimize the role and function of institutions within the regional government environment related to carrying out prevention and handling of protection of women from acts of violence;
to provide facilities and infrastructure;
to conduct guidance, supervision and evaluation.

Article 20
Regional governments are obligated to conduct guidance and supervision of the implementation of protection for women victims of violence.
Guidance as referred to in paragraph (1), includes: Guidelines and fulfillment standards;
Technical guidance and training;
Provision of facilities;
Monitoring;
Evaluation.
Guidance as referred to in paragraph (2), is intended to realize the protection of women from acts of violence in accordance with minimum service standards implemented by SKPD and the community.
SKPD as referred to in paragraph (3) is the Regional Work Unit within the Regional Government of Paser Regency that is related to the protection of women against acts of violence.

7.3.text:
CHAPTER VII
COMMUNITY PARTICIPATION
Article 17
The community can participate in prevention and handling efforts for women victims of violence through individuals or institutions.
Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) is implemented through: providing information and/or reporting any potential violence and incidents of violence that become known;
conducting prevention against the occurrence of acts of violence against women;
providing protection services to women who become victims of violence;
assisting in the process of repatriation, social rehabilitation, and social reintegration of women victims of acts of violence.

